n__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/772446-mystery-science-theater-3000-reborn?p=772784#post772784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MST3K has host segments, invention exchange, etc. that's absent from the setup and concept for RiffTrax.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be completely honest, as much as I love me some MST3K, and prefer Joel to Mike...those were my least favorite bits of the show. I'm sure I'm not theonly one who skips those bits in favor of just getting on with the MSTing!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well its going to be a new cast actually, but apparently the invitation is going to go out to all the former cast to come back and be writers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't been keeping up with RiffTrax, but a friend of mine has, and considers it at least as good as MST. In fact, he openly wonders why Joel doesn't just go to *them* and join up, instead of doing his own thing! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T08:05:03-08:00","id":779818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/772446-mystery-science-theater-3000-reborn?p=779786#post779786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't been keeping up with RiffTrax, but a friend of mine has, and considers it at least as good as MST. In fact, he openly wonders why Joel doesn't just go to *them* and join up, instead of doing his own thing!</div> </div> </div> </div>He actually tackled that in one of his updates. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joel Hodgson</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>4. Cinematic Titanic and Rifftrax are great. Who needs new <i>MST3K</i>?</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> To me, this has been the <i>weirdest</i> question to try and answer, because some people are acting like we're asking you to choose <i>between</i> Cinematic Titanic, Rifftrax and <i>MST3K</i>, or to convince you that <i>MST3K</i> is the &quot;one true riffing show.&quot; And guys, this might be why we can't have nice things.<br /> With <a href=\"http://www.rifftrax.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><u><span style=\"color:#0000ff\">Rifftrax</span></u></a>, Mike, Bill and Kevin have brought riffing to a whole new set of movies, by finding a way to riff the kinds of flicks we were never able to include in \u2013 or afford for \u2013 <i>MST3K</i>. And they're great at it!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.cinematictitanic.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b><u><span style=\"color:#0000ff\">Cinematic Titanic</span></u></b></a> was all about a live riffing experience that performers could share with fans in the house. It was an incredible thing to be part of, and even with so many great <i>MST3K</i> veterans involved, it still had a completely different flavor.<br /> <br /> I will <i>always</i> support good riffing, and the world will always need more riffing \u2013 especially under the imminent Trump/Carson Administration. Plus, it's exciting to watch so many <i>MST3K</i> vets out there doing their thing, and making people laugh, in whatever form they enjoy most. We're better off with more riffing shows out in the wild \u2013 and even if our old team comes back, they'll still be free to continue their other projects.<br /> <br /> But I know there's still a place for <i>Mystery Science Theater 3000</i> right there next to them, because the world will be more fun \u2013 and more bearable \u2013 with Crow, Servo, the Mads, and more cheesy B-movies.<br /> <br /> <b>No one is asking you to pick <i>between</i> Rifftrax and <i>MST3K</i>, and no one ever will. There's room for both of them.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, and also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joel Hodgson</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>5. Is there really a Santa Claus?</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Droppo, you are the laziest man on Mars.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T04:51:32-08:00","id":783374,"title":"","content":"Joel has started going through a list of the people who are offering their time and talent to the new series. Way too many to go through but the one that caught my eye was that Adam Savage has agreed to consult for their more ambitious camera shots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T07:32:50-08:00","id":783433,"title":"","content":"Thinking of the $85 reward now. I dunno. How are they gonna releasd it when it's made? Online I assume?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}